GetIntroductionContent() {
    content := FormatHeader("INTRODUCTION")
    content .= "Beacon is an accessibility-first tutorial and keyboard shortcuts system for Windows. It provides quick access to organized shortcut references for dozens of applications, Windows features, web apps, and assistive technologies without requiring you to leave your current workflow.`n`n"
    content .= "-- What Beacon Covers --`n"
    content .= "- Microsoft Office desktop and web apps, including Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook, OneNote, OneDrive, SharePoint, and Teams.`n"
    content .= "- Google Workspace apps, including Docs, Sheets, Slides, Gmail, Meet, Drive, and Calendar.`n"
    content .= "- Windows built-in apps and system tools, including File Explorer, Settings, Calculator, Notepad, Paint, Photos, Snipping Tool, Task Manager, Command Prompt, PowerShell, and Windows Terminal.`n"
    content .= "- Web browsers, communication tools, multimedia apps, PDF tools, developer tools, and productivity programs.`n"
    content .= "- Accessibility and assistive technology guides for JAWS, NVDA, Windows Narrator, Magnifier, ZoomText, Voice Access, Dragon, Read&Write, SuperNova, MAGic, and related combinations.`n`n"
    content .= "-- Accessibility-First Design --`n"
    content .= "- Full keyboard navigation through menus, guide windows, search boxes, and results.`n"
    content .= "- Screen reader friendly text output for JAWS, NVDA, Windows Narrator, and other assistive technologies.`n"
    content .= "- Automatic light and dark theme support for better visual comfort.`n"
    content .= "- Searchable shortcut guides with organized categories for faster lookup.`n"
    content .= "- Context-aware shortcut lookup for supported applications and accessibility-tool combinations.`n`n"
    content .= "-- How to Use Beacon --`n"
    content .= "Note: The Backtick key is also called the grave accent, grave, back quote, or tilde key. On most U.S. keyboards, it is directly below Esc and to the left of 1. It usually shares a key with Tilde (~).`n"
    content .= "1. Open the main Beacon menu with Windows + Shift + H, or use Backtick + 1 as a legacy fallback.`n"
    content .= "2. Use arrow keys or the mouse to move through categories and submenus.`n"
    content .= "3. Select a guide to open its keyboard shortcut reference.`n"
    content .= "4. Use the search box to filter a guide. Press Enter from the search box to return to the results area, then use arrow keys to review matches.`n"
    content .= "5. Press Escape or activate Close to leave a guide and return to your work.`n"
    content .= "6. Use Windows + Shift + K to auto-detect the focused app, or use Backtick + 2 as a legacy fallback.`n`n"
    content .= "-- Settings and Startup --`n"
    content .= "- Open Settings from the Beacon menu to add optional custom hotkeys for the main menu and auto-detect shortcut lookup.`n"
    content .= "- Settings can also enable or disable launching Beacon automatically when Windows starts.`n"
    content .= "- Announce Commands can be enabled in Settings to speak recognized shortcut commands as you use supported applications. It can follow the Windows default audio output, prefer a headphones/headset/Bluetooth output, use the Windows/SAPI default, or use a chosen output device. It respects Windows endpoint and app mixer volume settings, follows detected NVDA, JAWS, or Narrator speaking rates when available, can monitor screen-reader audio before speaking or experimentally speak before replaying recognized modifier shortcuts, recognizes common Windows global commands such as Alt + Tab, Alt + F4, and Windows + M, and lets Control stop Beacon speech without blocking the Control key.`n"
    content .= "- The built-in hotkeys remain available even if you do not configure extra hotkeys.`n`n"
    content .= "-- System Requirements --`n"
    content .= "- Windows 10 or Windows 11.`n"
    content .= "- The compiled Beacon.exe version includes its required files.`n"
    content .= "- The script version requires AutoHotkey v2.0 or later, with Beacon.ahk and content.ahk in the same folder.`n`n"
    content .= "-- Support --`n"
    content .= "For help, suggestions, or updates, visit EyeTech Analytics at https://eyetechanalytics.com/beacon/ or contact richard@eyetechanalytics.com.`n"
    return content
}

GetModifierKeysContent() {
    content := FormatHeader("KEYBOARD MODIFIER KEYS")
    content .= "-- Standard Modifier Keys --`n"
    content .= "Ctrl:       Control key - used for common commands`n"
    content .= "Alt:        Alternate key - activates menu commands`n"
    content .= "Shift:      Used to type uppercase or alternate characters`n"
    content .= "Windows:    Opens Start menu or activates Windows commands`n"
    content .= "Apps/Menu:  Activates context menu (same as right-click)`n`n"
    content .= "-- Special Keys --`n"
    content .= "Esc:          Escape - cancels operations or closes dialogs`n"
    content .= "Tab:          Tabulation - moves between fields or indents text`n"
    content .= "Caps Lock:    Toggles all letters to uppercase when typing`n"
    content .= "Num Lock:     Toggles number pad between numbers and navigation`n"
    content .= "Scroll Lock:  Rarely used legacy function, changes arrow key behavior in some programs`n"
    content .= "Insert:       Toggles between insert and overwrite mode`n"
    content .= "Delete:       Removes character after cursor or selected content`n"
    content .= "Backspace:    Removes character before cursor`n"
    content .= "Enter:        Confirms action or creates new line`n`n"
    content .= "-- Function Keys --`n"
    content .= "F1:  Help`n"
    content .= "F2:  Rename selected item (in Windows)`n"
    content .= "F3:  Search`n"
    content .= "F4:  Repeat last action (in some applications)`n"
    content .= "F5:  Refresh or Run`n"
    content .= "F6:  Move to address bar (in browsers)`n"
    content .= "F10: Activate menu bar`n"
    content .= "F11: Full screen mode (in browsers)`n"
    content .= "F12: Developer tools (in browsers) or Save As (in MS Office)`n`n"
    content .= "-- Key Combinations in AutoHotkey --`n"
    content .= "^  Represents the Ctrl key`n"
    content .= "!  Represents the Alt key`n"
    content .= "+  Represents the Shift key`n"
    content .= "#  Represents the Windows key`n"
    content .= "&  Used to combine two keys for a custom hotkey`n"
    return content
}

GetClipboardShortcutContent() {
    content := FormatHeader("CLIPBOARD KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS")
    content .= "-- Standard Clipboard Operations --`n"
    content .= "Ctrl + C:                         Copy the selected item(s) to the clipboard.`n"
    content .= "Ctrl + X or Shift + Delete: Cut the selected item(s) to the clipboard.`n"
    content .= "Ctrl + V or Shift + Insert: Paste the most recent item from the clipboard.`n"
    content .= "Ctrl + Z:                         Undo the last action (often includes paste).`n"
    content .= "Print Screen (PrtScn):        Copy a screenshot of the entire screen to the clipboard.`n"
    content .= "Alt + Print Screen:             Copy a screenshot of the active window to the clipboard.`n`n"

    content .= "-- Windows Clipboard History (Windows 10 October 2018 Update and later) --`n"
    content .= "Note: Clipboard history must be enabled in Windows Settings (Settings > System > Clipboard).`n`n"
    content .= "Windows key + V:              Open Clipboard History panel. You can then select an item to paste.`n"
    content .= "  - In Clipboard History panel:`n"
    content .= "    - Arrow keys:             Navigate through clipboard items.`n"
    content .= "    - Enter:                  Paste the selected item.`n"
    content .= "    - Delete:                 Delete the selected item from history.`n"
    content .= "    - Tab / Shift + Tab:      Navigate between items and options (e.g., Pin, Clear all).`n"
    content .= "    - P (when item selected): Pin the selected item so it's not removed when history clears or PC restarts.`n"
    content .= "    - C (when item selected, if 'Clear all' is focused): Clear all unpinned items from history.`n`n"

    content .= "-- Snipping Tool / Snip & Sketch --`n"
    content .= "Windows key + Shift + S:    Open Snip & Sketch (or the older Snipping Tool selection UI) to capture a region of your screen to the clipboard.`n"
    content .= "  Options typically include Rectangular Snip, Freeform Snip, Window Snip, and Fullscreen Snip.`n`n"

    content .= "-- Office Clipboard (Microsoft Office Applications) --`n"
    content .= "Office applications have their own clipboard pane that can store multiple items.`n"
    content .= "Ctrl + C (twice quickly):   May open the Office Clipboard pane in some versions/configurations.`n"
    content .= "Access via Home tab > Clipboard group (click the dialog launcher arrow).`n`n"

    content .= "Tip: Many applications allow you to right-click to access Cut, Copy, and Paste commands via a context menu.`n"
