GetMAGic_GeneralATContent() {
    content := "-- Overview --`n"
    content .= "MAGic is a screen magnification tool from Freedom Scientific (the`n"
    content .= "makers of JAWS). When JAWS and MAGic are both licensed, they can`n"
    content .= "operate simultaneously as 'Freedom Scientific FUSION'. MAGic alone`n"
    content .= "provides optional limited speech but is primarily a magnifier.`n`n"
    content .= "-- Core Magnification Shortcuts --`n"
    content .= "Ctrl + Num+:            Increase magnification`n"
    content .= "Ctrl + Num-:            Decrease magnification`n"
    content .= "MAGic Key + Enter:      Toggle magnification on/off`n`n"
    content .= "-- Running MAGic with JAWS --`n"
    content .= "Both sets of keyboard shortcuts remain active. JAWS handles all`n"
    content .= "screen reading; MAGic handles all magnification. There are no`n"
    content .= "command conflicts by default.`n"
    content .= "If using FUSION, check the JAWS guide for reading shortcuts.`n`n"
    content .= "-- Running MAGic with NVDA --`n"
    content .= "MAGic and NVDA can run simultaneously. NVDA handles screen reading;`n"
    content .= "MAGic handles magnification. Both products are independent.`n"
    content .= "The MAGic Key modifier should not conflict with NVDA's Insert key.`n`n"
    content .= "-- MAGic Speech (limited) --`n"
    content .= "Alt + Delete:           Toggle MAGic speech on/off`n"
    content .= "MAGic Key + S:          Read current word`n"
    content .= "Disable MAGic speech if a dedicated screen reader is also running.`n"
    return content
}

